        "original_id": "e90ed412-1caf-523f-a189-fbf745fb45bc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Keith Morris, Rome Ramirez, Eric Wilson, Josh Freese\n- Bands: Black Flag, Circle Jerks, Off!, Sublime with Rome, Sublime, The Vandals, Dirty Heads\n- Songs: \"We've Had Enough\", \"Lay Me Down\"\n- Genres: hardcore punk, reggae rock\n- Charts: Billboard Alternative Songs, Billboard Rock Songs\n\nFacts:\n- Keith Morris was born on September 18, 1955, and he is an American singer and songwriter.\n- Keith Morris is known as the frontman of the hardcore punk bands Black Flag, Circle Jerks, and Off!.\n- Roman René Ramírez was born on June 11, 1988, in Fremont, California, and he is an American singer and guitarist.\n- Rome Ramirez is best known for performing with Eric Wilson from Sublime and Josh Freese from The Vandals in the band Sublime with Rome.\n- The song \"We've Had Enough\" features backing vocals by Keith Morris.\n- Keith Morris was the singer of Circle Jerks and the original singer of Black Flag.\n- In 2010, the Dirty Heads released the song \"Lay Me Down\" featuring Rome Ramirez from Sublime with Rome.\n- \"Lay Me Down\" reached number 1 on the Billboard Alternative Songs and Billboard Rock Songs charts.\n- The 2010 success of \"Lay Me Down\" boosted the popularity of the reggae rock genre.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
